973
00:34:14.180 --> 00:34:15.480
I think, well, here's the thing.
我想，嗯，是这样的。

974
00:34:15.580 --> 00:34:17.980
You asked what we did between our break, right?
你问我们休息的时候做了什么，对吧？

975
00:34:18.120 --> 00:34:18.180
Yeah.
对。

976
00:34:18.260 --> 00:34:21.780
You went and worked on that 70s show and have gossip you don't want to tell us.
你去拍了《70年代秀》，还有不想告诉我们的八卦。

977
00:34:23.420 --> 00:34:25.480
I was, you know, very much on a budget.
我当时，你知道，手头非常紧。

978
00:34:25.480 --> 00:34:28.540
I went back to working at the improv theater I was working at.
我回去我工作的即兴剧场上班了。

979
00:34:28.540 --> 00:34:36.180
I needed to, when we were going back to work, I needed to get my hair dyed because my hair, I'm like a sort of a dirty blonde, right?
我需要，当我们准备回去工作时，我得去染头发，因为我的头发，我算是那种深金色，对吧？

980
00:34:36.280 --> 00:34:37.060
A dishwater blonde.
那种洗碗水一样的金色。

981
00:34:37.060 --> 00:34:42.280
And I decided to dye my hair myself to save the money because it's really expensive.
我决定自己染头发来省钱，因为去店里真的很贵。

982
00:34:42.740 --> 00:34:42.840
Yeah.
是啊。

983
00:34:42.840 --> 00:34:47.860
So, I went to the drugstore and I got a home kit.
所以，我去了药店买了一套家用染发剂。

984
00:34:48.080 --> 00:34:55.000
And so, actually, I remember people wrote in on the comments section at IMDb, which you should never look at.
其实，我记得有人在IMDb的评论区留言，你永远不该去看那个。

985
00:34:55.160 --> 00:34:56.780
They wrote in and said, what happened?
他们写道，发生了什么？

986
00:34:56.800 --> 00:34:58.700
Why is her hair so bleach blonde?
为什么她的头发变得那么浅金？

987
00:34:59.020 --> 00:35:00.620
My hair is so blonde.
我的头发太金了。

988
00:35:00.620 --> 00:35:03.980
And I think that dang bug thought I was a flower.
我觉得那该死的虫子以为我是朵花。

989
00:35:05.520 --> 00:35:07.180
I dyed my hair myself.
我自己染的头发。

990
00:35:07.180 --> 00:35:07.920
Look at it.
你看。

991
00:35:08.020 --> 00:35:09.980
It's like, I think I burnt my scalp.
感觉就像，我觉得我把头皮都烧伤了。

992
00:35:10.500 --> 00:35:20.240
Well, John Krasinski started then doing this bit where he was pretending to be the bug, picking you up and carrying you away from all of us.
嗯，约翰·卡拉辛斯基当时开始玩这个梗，他假装自己是那只虫子，把我拎起来，带离我们所有人。

993
00:35:20.320 --> 00:35:21.640
And we'd be like, bye, Angela.
我们就会说，再见，安吉拉。

994
00:35:21.860 --> 00:35:23.720
And I'd be like, but he would like do this.
我会说，但他会这样……

995
00:35:23.860 --> 00:35:25.020
He's so tall, first of all.
首先，他个子太高了。

996
00:35:25.160 --> 00:35:31.240
He would like do his arms like, and then like attach to my shoulders and then like kind of pick me up and like drop me off.
他会把手臂像这样，然后抓住我的肩膀，接着把我拎起来，再把我放下。

997
00:35:31.440 --> 00:35:32.440
But here's the thing, guys.
但重点是，伙计们。

998
00:35:32.580 --> 00:35:34.900
I do not like people scaring me.
我不喜欢别人吓我。

999
00:35:34.920 --> 00:35:35.840
We've discussed this.
我们讨论过这个问题。

1000
00:35:36.080 --> 00:35:37.660
I like swat or hit.
我喜欢拍打或击打。

1001
00:35:37.860 --> 00:35:39.480
I also don't like anything near my ears.
我也不喜欢任何东西靠近我的耳朵。

1002
00:35:39.480 --> 00:35:40.960
My ears were already sunburned.
我的耳朵当时已经晒伤了。

1003
00:35:41.120 --> 00:35:41.380
Yeah.
没错。

1004
00:35:41.540 --> 00:35:44.580
And this thing would buzz by my ears and I would shriek and flail about.
那东西会在我耳边嗡嗡作响，我会尖叫着乱挥乱舞。

1005
00:35:44.800 --> 00:35:46.060
And I think I did ruin the take.
我想我确实毁了那次拍摄。

1006
00:35:46.140 --> 00:35:54.800
And then I remember that John, as a joke, decided to come up right next to your ear and pretend to be the bug.
然后我记得约翰开玩笑说，他决定凑到你耳边假装是那只虫子。

1007
00:35:54.920 --> 00:35:55.820
Make the buzz noise.
发出嗡嗡声。

1008
00:35:56.060 --> 00:35:59.320
And you were so startled, you hit him in the face.
结果你吓了一跳，直接给了他一拳。

1009
00:35:59.440 --> 00:36:00.820
I hit him as hard as I could.
我用尽全力打了他。

1010
00:36:00.980 --> 00:36:02.900
I didn't know I was going to be hitting John.
我当时不知道我会打到约翰。

1011
00:36:03.060 --> 00:36:04.580
No, you had your thing.
不，你有你的反应。

1012
00:36:04.580 --> 00:36:05.780
You had your reaction.
你有你的本能反应。

1013
00:36:06.120 --> 00:36:08.460
So a lot was going on in the background.
所以背景里发生了很多事。

1014
00:36:08.460 --> 00:36:15.300
I have a question because at 16 minutes, 12 seconds, you guys, Roy is waving about.
我有个问题，因为在16分12秒的时候，你们看，罗伊在挥手。

1015
00:36:15.880 --> 00:36:21.060
David Dinman is waving his hand back and forth and he kind of jumps up and down.
大卫·丁曼在来回挥手，还跳上跳下的。

1016
00:36:21.240 --> 00:36:23.760
And I couldn't help but wonder if it was the bug.
我不禁想，那是不是因为那只虫子。

1017
00:36:23.760 --> 00:36:25.440
That's amazing.
太神奇了。

1018
00:36:26.020 --> 00:36:34.120
I have to talk about the talking head where we learned that Michael lost all of his money in a pyramid scheme.
我得聊聊那个采访片段，我们得知迈克尔在传销骗局中赔光了所有钱。

1019
00:36:34.260 --> 00:36:34.660
Oh.
噢。

1020
00:36:35.200 --> 00:36:39.420
And he says it was okay because it taught him more than he could have learned in business school.
他说没关系，因为这让他学到的比商学院里学到的还要多。

1021
00:36:40.080 --> 00:36:40.480
Yes.
是的。

1022
00:36:40.800 --> 00:36:44.740
It was just – I have nothing to say about it except for that I thought it was a great talking head.
这简直——我对此无话可说，除了我觉得那是个很棒的采访片段。

1023
00:36:44.740 --> 00:36:45.160
I know.
我知道。

1024
00:36:45.300 --> 00:36:50.820
Well, Michael has a line in this episode for me that is just one of those lines that sums up Michael.
嗯，迈克尔在这一集里有一句台词，对我来说，那句台词完美概括了迈克尔。

1025
00:36:51.000 --> 00:36:53.360
Michael is in Ryan's car in the backseat with Ryan.
迈克尔和瑞安坐在瑞安的车后座上。

1026
00:36:53.580 --> 00:36:56.280
Ryan feels totally uncomfortable the majority of this episode.
瑞安在这一集的大部分时间里都感到非常不自在。

1027
00:36:56.280 --> 00:37:00.520
But Michael says to Ryan, I became a salesman because of people.
但迈克尔对瑞安说，我成为销售员是因为喜欢人。

1028
00:37:00.520 --> 00:37:02.180
I love making friends.
我喜欢交朋友。

1029
00:37:02.520 --> 00:37:02.800
Oh.
噢。

1030
00:37:03.580 --> 00:37:04.000
Oh.
噢。

1031
00:37:04.180 --> 00:37:11.500
And I think he probably was a good salesman, but he's horrible in management because he doesn't get to, like, you know, butter up strangers.
我觉得他可能确实是个好销售，但他做管理很糟糕，因为他没法像以前那样去讨好陌生人了。

1032
00:37:11.880 --> 00:37:14.660
Well, we see him be a great salesman in future episodes.
嗯，我们在以后的剧集里看到他是个出色的销售。

1033
00:37:14.840 --> 00:37:17.460
So he was very good at that and then got promoted to manager.
所以他很擅长那个，然后被提拔成了经理。

1034
00:37:17.720 --> 00:37:18.920
And now I think he's lonely.
而现在我觉得他很孤独。

1035
00:37:18.920 --> 00:37:24.460
My next fan question has to do with the scene where Dwight is pouting in his car.
我的下一个粉丝提问是关于德怀特在车里生闷气的那场戏。

1036
00:37:24.700 --> 00:37:25.520
Oh, yes.
噢，对。

1037
00:37:25.520 --> 00:37:27.360
Let's do that because I have a card about that.
我们聊聊那个，因为我正好有张关于那场戏的卡片。

1038
00:37:27.500 --> 00:37:27.700
Great.
太好了。

1039
00:37:28.060 --> 00:37:35.980
So Lucy asked, how many takes did it take for the scene where you and John are helping Dwight with his emotions when he's listening to REM in his car?
露西问，你和约翰在德怀特车里听REM乐队的歌时帮他处理情绪，那场戏拍了多少次？

1040
00:37:36.620 --> 00:37:39.200
Rain seems to almost break at the end of that scene.
雷恩在结尾处好像快要笑场了。

1041
00:37:40.020 --> 00:37:43.280
Are you and John's reactions authentic or scripted?
你和约翰的反应是真实的还是照着剧本演的？

1042
00:37:44.240 --> 00:37:45.680
Well, it took a lot of takes.
嗯，拍了很多次。

1043
00:37:45.680 --> 00:37:46.480
I'll say that.
我只能说这么多。

1044
00:37:46.680 --> 00:37:47.840
We spent a lot of time on that scene.
我们在那场戏上花了很多时间。

1045
00:37:47.840 --> 00:37:50.780
I mean, I'm sorry, you were probably in the background with the bug on that one, Angela.
我是说，抱歉，安吉拉，你当时可能还在背景里对付那只虫子吧。

1046
00:37:51.000 --> 00:37:53.120
I was probably fending for my life back there.
我当时可能正在后面拼命自保呢。

1047
00:37:53.520 --> 00:37:54.880
Me and Roy, apparently.
显然还有我和罗伊。

1048
00:37:55.160 --> 00:37:57.120
And yes, I think rain is almost breaking.
是的，我觉得雷恩确实快要笑场了。

1049
00:37:57.560 --> 00:38:05.320
I think rain is almost breaking at the end, but I actually wrote this, and I know my jam people out there are not going to be happy, but I said at 14, 22 seconds,
我觉得雷恩在结尾处快要笑场了，但我其实写了这个，我知道我的“吉姆和帕姆”粉丝们可能不会高兴，但我说在14分22秒的时候，

1050
00:38:05.520 --> 00:38:07.740
I thought Jim and Pam were being mean to Dwight.
我觉得吉姆和帕姆对德怀特太刻薄了。

1051
00:38:07.840 --> 00:38:08.340
I agree.
我同意。

1052
00:38:08.620 --> 00:38:11.080
When I watched this episode, I didn't like us.
我看这一集的时候，不喜欢我们当时的表现。

1053
00:38:11.200 --> 00:38:12.580
I didn't like you guys there either.
我当时也不喜欢你们在那里的表现。

1054
00:38:12.720 --> 00:38:15.220
In fact, Jim suggests that he quits.
事实上，吉姆提议他辞职。

1055
00:38:15.520 --> 00:38:15.780
Yeah.
是啊。

1056
00:38:16.100 --> 00:38:16.400
You know?
你知道吗？

1057
00:38:16.540 --> 00:38:17.160
I didn't like it.
我不喜欢那样。

1058
00:38:17.160 --> 00:38:19.240
And then you guys laugh as you walk away.
然后你们走开的时候还在笑。

1059
00:38:19.360 --> 00:38:20.180
And here's the thing.
关键是这样。

1060
00:38:20.280 --> 00:38:25.120
I don't mind when you do pranks in the office because Dwight is so ridiculous, and he takes himself way too seriously.
我不介意你们在办公室搞恶作剧，因为德怀特太荒唐了，而且他太把自己当回事了。

1061
00:38:25.440 --> 00:38:30.800
But in this episode, his feelings had been hurt, and he was feeling sad and kind of rejected.
但在这一集里，他受伤了，感到难过，还有点被排斥的感觉。

1062
00:38:31.080 --> 00:38:31.300
Yeah.
是啊。

1063
00:38:31.300 --> 00:38:36.080
And I thought you guys were doing jokes at his expense, and I didn't like it.
我觉得你们是在拿他开涮，我不喜欢这样。

1064
00:38:36.300 --> 00:38:36.720
Me either.
我也不喜欢。

1065
00:38:36.720 --> 00:38:38.120
I thought we crossed a line.
我觉得我们越界了。

1066
00:38:38.320 --> 00:38:38.480
Yep.
没错。

1067
00:38:38.680 --> 00:38:48.880
You know, something that I like about our show is that we were whole characters, and as people in your whole life, you probably aren't great every moment, right?
你知道，我喜欢我们这部剧的一点是，我们塑造的是完整的人物，就像现实生活中的人一样，你不可能每时每刻都表现得很好，对吧？

1068
00:38:48.960 --> 00:38:50.880
Well, you have moments you're not proud of that you were like, you know what?
嗯，你总会有一些让你感到不光彩的时刻，你会想，你知道吗？

1069
00:38:50.880 --> 00:38:51.980
I could have been better in that moment.
在那一刻我本可以做得更好。

1070
00:38:52.140 --> 00:38:52.380
Yes.
是的。

1071
00:38:52.500 --> 00:38:54.720
And I thought Jim and Pam could have been better in that moment.
我觉得吉姆和帕姆在那一刻本可以做得更好。

1072
00:38:54.920 --> 00:38:55.020
Yeah.
是啊。

1073
00:38:55.020 --> 00:38:56.200
I was disappointed in them.
我对他们感到失望。

1074
00:38:56.920 --> 00:39:05.140
Camille also asked, a couple of episodes ago, you mentioned that the cars we see your characters drive are sometimes your actual cars.
卡米尔还问过，几集之前，你们提到过剧中角色开的车有时是你们自己的车。

1075
00:39:05.360 --> 00:39:08.020
Is the car that Dwight listens to?
那辆德怀特听歌的车呢？

1076
00:39:08.540 --> 00:39:09.560
Everybody Hurts.
《每个人都会受伤》那首？

1077
00:39:09.680 --> 00:39:10.000
Yes.
是的。

1078
00:39:10.200 --> 00:39:11.280
Is that Rain's actual car?
那是雷恩自己的车吗？

1079
00:39:11.420 --> 00:39:11.820
No.
不是。

1080
00:39:12.120 --> 00:39:14.100
That was a Dwight car.
那是德怀特的车。

1081
00:39:14.280 --> 00:39:14.560
Yes.
是的。

1082
00:39:14.560 --> 00:39:15.640
We bought that just for Dwight.
那是我们专门为德怀特买的。

1083
00:39:15.760 --> 00:39:20.260
And also, Michael Sebring, they rented that just for Michael.
还有迈克尔的赛百灵，那是专门为迈克尔租的。

1084
00:39:20.440 --> 00:39:20.900
That's right.
没错。

1085
00:39:20.900 --> 00:39:26.980
And we only used our cars in some of those few first episodes, and really after that, I think we got a bigger budget.
我们只在前几集用了自己的车，在那之后，我想我们的预算变多了。

1086
00:39:27.600 --> 00:39:27.820
Yes.
是的。

1087
00:39:27.920 --> 00:39:31.000
Pam had a Kia, I think, for a while, and they rented that.
帕姆有一段时间开的是起亚，那是租来的。

1088
00:39:31.040 --> 00:39:32.640
So they rented all these cars for us.
所以他们为我们租了所有这些车。

1089
00:39:32.820 --> 00:39:37.000
What about the warehouse guys breaking bottles in the background?
那仓库员工在背景里砸瓶子是怎么回事？

1090
00:39:37.000 --> 00:39:38.720
I have that on a card.
我卡片上有这一条。

1091
00:39:38.940 --> 00:39:41.960
So the warehouse guys look like they're smashing beer bottles.
仓库员工看起来像是在砸啤酒瓶。

1092
00:39:42.060 --> 00:39:42.580
And you know what?
而且你知道吗？

1093
00:39:42.580 --> 00:39:50.000
It actually even annoys Roy, which is Roy's motivation to come over to you and be like, gosh, you know those warehouse guys.
这甚至让罗伊感到烦恼，这也是罗伊过来找你们的原因，他想说，天哪，你们知道那些仓库员工是怎么回事吗。

1094
00:39:50.000 --> 00:39:53.420
Like, he actually almost seemed vulnerable to me in that moment.
那一刻他看起来甚至有点脆弱。

1095
00:39:53.580 --> 00:39:53.840
He did.
确实。

1096
00:39:53.840 --> 00:39:55.500
That, like, he didn't want to hang out with them.
就好像他不想和他们待在一起一样。

1097
00:39:55.620 --> 00:39:59.180
And I thought it was sort of weird that he was like, can I hang out with you guys?
我觉得他问“我能和你们待在一起吗”有点奇怪。

1098
00:39:59.300 --> 00:39:59.540
Yeah.
是啊。

1099
00:39:59.700 --> 00:40:01.040
Can you hang out with your own girlfriend?
你就不能和你自己的女朋友待在一起吗？

1100
00:40:01.040 --> 00:40:01.880
I think you can.
我想你是可以的。

1101
00:40:02.180 --> 00:40:02.420
Yeah.
是啊。

1102
00:40:02.640 --> 00:40:02.760
Fiance.
未婚夫。

1103
00:40:03.260 --> 00:40:03.660
Fiance.
未婚夫。

1104
00:40:03.900 --> 00:40:04.500
Look, see?
看，看到了吗？

1105
00:40:04.680 --> 00:40:05.160
I know.
我知道。

1106
00:40:05.340 --> 00:40:07.500
I actually kind of liked seeing Roy like that.
其实我挺喜欢看罗伊那样的。

1107
00:40:07.640 --> 00:40:08.520
I liked seeing him.
我喜欢见到他。

1108
00:40:08.620 --> 00:40:10.580
But then he so quickly is a turd again.
但转眼间他又变回了那个混蛋。

1109
00:40:10.800 --> 00:40:14.920
Well, I guess you did like seeing him, Angela, because during the game, who would you do?
好吧，我想你确实喜欢见到他，安吉拉，因为在游戏过程中，你会选谁？

1110
00:40:15.040 --> 00:40:16.020
He says, Angela.
他说，安吉拉。

1111
00:40:16.380 --> 00:40:17.600
I didn't say Roy.
我没说罗伊。

1112
00:40:17.600 --> 00:40:21.240
No, but there was a fan question under construction.
不，但当时有个粉丝提问正在准备中。

1113
00:40:21.240 --> 00:40:23.280
Who would Angela's character do?
安吉拉的角色会选谁？

1114
00:40:24.180 --> 00:40:26.580
Angela, would it have been Dwight or Roy?
安吉拉，会是德怀特还是罗伊？

1115
00:40:26.860 --> 00:40:27.920
It would have been a toss up.
这很难说。

1116
00:40:28.020 --> 00:40:31.420
I would have liked to seen them fight over me and be titillated.
我本来想看他们为我争风吃醋，那会让我很兴奋。

1117
00:40:32.980 --> 00:40:34.820
And then I would have picked the winner.
然后我会选赢的那个人。

1118
00:40:35.300 --> 00:40:38.180
Well, all of the women say Jim, except for Pam.
好吧，所有的女士都选了吉姆，除了帕姆。

1119
00:40:38.460 --> 00:40:40.340
Pam says Oscar or Toby.
帕姆选了奥斯卡或者托比。

1120
00:40:40.340 --> 00:40:44.460
Now, she's obviously saying this because she doesn't want to admit Jim.
显然她这么说是为了不想承认选吉姆。

1121
