00:46:07.860 --> 00:46:12.320
I don't like how Pam then snarkily laughs at Katie.
我不喜欢帕姆随后嘲讽地笑凯蒂的样子。

1286
00:46:12.560 --> 00:46:13.500
When she says it.
就在她说出那部电影的时候。

1287
00:46:13.600 --> 00:46:14.460
I don't like it.
我不喜欢那样。

1288
00:46:14.540 --> 00:46:15.560
I thought it was catty.
我觉得这很刻薄。

1289
00:46:15.660 --> 00:46:16.660
I thought it was competitive.
我觉得这是一种竞争心态。

1290
00:46:17.120 --> 00:46:21.620
And I know that she's jealous of Katie, but Pam likes Legally Blonde.
我知道她嫉妒凯蒂，但帕姆明明喜欢《律政俏佳人》。

1291
00:46:22.140 --> 00:46:24.260
So why can't she just say that to Jim?
所以她为什么不能直接对吉姆说呢？

1292
00:46:24.260 --> 00:46:24.740
I know.
我知道。

1293
00:46:24.900 --> 00:46:26.200
She doesn't stand up for herself.
她没有坚持自己的立场。

1294
00:46:26.380 --> 00:46:30.120
And then she shames Katie for it because she's trying to look cool for Jim.
然后她还因为想在吉姆面前装酷，而去羞辱凯蒂。

1295
00:46:30.200 --> 00:46:31.580
And I think it's a flaw.
我觉得这是一个缺点。

1296
00:46:32.180 --> 00:46:32.820
I do.
确实是。

1297
00:46:32.980 --> 00:46:37.640
And I like it because I think it shows Pam being human and complex, but it does make me cringe.
我喜欢这个设定，因为它展现了帕姆人性化和复杂的一面，但这确实让我感到尴尬。

1298
00:46:37.860 --> 00:46:40.080
I remember dating a guy in college.
我记得大学时和一个男生约会过。

1299
00:46:40.580 --> 00:46:41.420
Oh, my God.
天哪。

1300
00:46:41.420 --> 00:46:43.320
He loved the show Bass Masters.
他特别喜欢《鲈鱼大师》那个节目。

1301
00:46:44.140 --> 00:46:46.440
Guys, I don't give a crap about.
伙计们，我根本不在乎。

1302
00:46:46.820 --> 00:46:47.260
Sorry.
抱歉。

1303
00:46:47.760 --> 00:46:48.360
I don't.
我真的不在乎。

1304
00:46:48.440 --> 00:46:49.240
Here's the thing.
重点是这样的。

1305
00:46:49.240 --> 00:46:51.680
I appreciate that you want to get out in nature.
我很欣赏你们想去亲近大自然的心情。

1306
00:46:52.020 --> 00:46:53.660
I don't need to watch you fish.
但我不需要看你们钓鱼。

1307
00:46:53.980 --> 00:46:56.280
No offense to the Bass Master people.
并不是对那些钓鱼大师赛的人有什么意见。

1308
00:46:56.320 --> 00:47:02.420
But I would watch hours of Bass Master with this guy in college because I liked him.
但我大学时确实陪这家伙看了好几个小时的钓鱼比赛，因为我喜欢他。

1309
00:47:02.800 --> 00:47:04.020
And I'm like, oh, my God.
当时我就想，天哪。

1310
00:47:04.020 --> 00:47:04.740
No, I think that's different.
不，我觉得那不一样。

1311
00:47:04.900 --> 00:47:06.480
Well, I think you edited yourself.
嗯，我觉得你当时是在刻意伪装自己。

1312
00:47:06.700 --> 00:47:11.460
I think Pam, not Jenna, edited herself for Jim because she likes him.
我觉得是帕姆，而不是珍娜，为了吉姆刻意伪装了自己，因为她喜欢他。

1313
00:47:11.560 --> 00:47:14.780
But what I don't like is that it was at the expense of Meredith.
但我不喜欢的是，这牺牲了梅雷迪思的感受。

1314
00:47:14.780 --> 00:47:21.580
You, like, Jim judged Meredith's picks, and then he judged you, and then you judged Katie.
你看，吉姆评判了梅雷迪思的选择，然后他评判了你，接着你又评判了凯蒂。

1315
00:47:21.820 --> 00:47:22.260
Exactly.
没错。

1316
00:47:22.260 --> 00:47:23.260
That's what I'm saying.
我说的就是这个意思。

1317
00:47:23.480 --> 00:47:25.500
Like, that's the sort of behavior that I didn't like.
那种行为是我所不喜欢的。

1318
00:47:25.620 --> 00:47:29.940
I dated a lot of people where I took on their interests because I like them.
我以前约会过很多人，为了讨好他们，我会去培养他们的兴趣爱好。

1319
00:47:29.980 --> 00:47:30.900
I think that's love.
我觉得这就是爱。

1320
00:47:31.080 --> 00:47:38.620
You know, I think, you know, I will get up in the middle of the night and watch the World Cup with my husband because he loves it.
你知道，我觉得，我会为了陪我丈夫看世界杯而在半夜起床，因为他热爱这项运动。

1321
00:47:38.620 --> 00:47:40.540
You know, I think that's cool.
你知道，我觉得这很酷。

1322
00:47:40.680 --> 00:47:45.900
But anyway, after all of this happens, Pam kisses Roy in front of Jim.
但不管怎样，在这一切发生之后，帕姆在吉姆面前吻了罗伊。

1323
00:47:46.180 --> 00:47:46.520
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1324
00:47:46.720 --> 00:47:47.880
You want to see what I wrote?
你想看看我写了什么吗？

1325
00:47:48.060 --> 00:47:48.320
What?
什么？

1326
00:47:48.680 --> 00:47:54.580
First of all, I said at 19 minutes, 52 seconds, we have some serious Pam sass happening.
首先，我在19分52秒处写道，帕姆表现得非常刻薄。

1327
00:47:54.860 --> 00:47:57.600
She laughs when Katie also says Legally Blonde.
当凯蒂也说《律政俏佳人》时，她笑了。

1328
00:47:57.760 --> 00:48:06.740
And then she says, what an adorable car, which is basically Pam's moment of looks like someone took the slow train to Philly.
然后她说，多可爱的车啊，这基本上就是帕姆在说别人反应迟钝。

1329
00:48:07.260 --> 00:48:08.720
This is Pam's moment.
这是帕姆的高光时刻。

1330
00:48:09.120 --> 00:48:11.380
Like, she is being so snarky.
她当时真的太尖酸刻薄了。

1331
00:48:11.460 --> 00:48:11.820
I know.
我知道。

1332
00:48:12.080 --> 00:48:16.960
And then I put, and then Pam smooches Roy in front of everyone.
然后我写道，帕姆在大家面前亲吻了罗伊。

1333
00:48:17.520 --> 00:48:18.080
Tacky.
俗气。

1334
00:48:18.300 --> 00:48:21.900
Oh, you wrote tacky because I wrote, okay, I would do that.
哦，你写了俗气，因为我写的是，好吧，我会那么做。

1335
00:48:22.100 --> 00:48:22.580
Tacky.
俗气。

1336
00:48:22.780 --> 00:48:32.220
I wouldn't throw, like, someone else's opinions under the bus and change all my way I think to impress a man.
我不会为了讨好男人而贬低别人的观点，也不会改变自己的想法。

1337
00:48:32.480 --> 00:48:36.200
But I would try to make him jealous by kissing someone else.
但我会通过亲吻别人来让他吃醋。

1338
00:48:37.920 --> 00:48:39.280
I thought that I would do.
我以为我会那么做。

1339
00:48:39.440 --> 00:48:40.540
I said tacky.
我写了俗气。

1340
00:48:40.760 --> 00:48:44.120
And I want to say two fans wrote in about this as well.
我想说，也有两位粉丝写信提到了这一点。

1341
00:48:44.580 --> 00:48:49.480
Macy said, can we all agree that in this episode, Jim is completely wrong about Legally Blonde.
梅西说，我们能达成共识吗？在这一集中，吉姆对《律政俏佳人》的看法完全错了。

1342
00:48:49.580 --> 00:48:50.540
It's a great movie.
那是一部很棒的电影。

1343
00:48:50.740 --> 00:48:52.100
Everyone was right to pick it.
大家选它都是对的。

1344
00:48:52.100 --> 00:48:53.580
And Chubby Bookworm said,
还有“胖书虫”说，

1345
00:48:53.800 --> 00:49:05.380
why is Jim so opposed to a movie about a girl who is strong enough to go for what she wants and along the way finds herself and encourages others and upbuilds them and is capable and inspiring?
为什么吉姆那么反对一部关于女孩的电影？她有勇气去追求自己想要的东西，在过程中找到了自我，鼓励了他人，提升了他人，而且既有能力又鼓舞人心。

1346
00:49:05.660 --> 00:49:06.720
I agree.
我同意。

1347
00:49:06.720 --> 00:49:08.840
I think Legally Blonde is a great movie.
我觉得《律政俏佳人》是一部很棒的电影。

1348
00:49:09.040 --> 00:49:09.880
It has a positive message.
它传达了积极的信息。

1349
00:49:10.460 --> 00:49:11.560
You heard it here.
你们都听到了。

1350
00:49:11.700 --> 00:49:12.020
Jim is wrong.
吉姆错了。

1351
00:49:12.320 --> 00:49:13.960
You heard it here, Reese Witherspoon.
你们都听到了，瑞茜·威瑟斯彭。

1352
00:49:15.200 --> 00:49:20.260
Yeah, Reese Witherspoon, in case you were worried that the movie didn't land.
没错，瑞茜·威瑟斯彭，以防你们担心这部电影没火起来。

1353
00:49:20.260 --> 00:49:21.460
And it landed.
它确实火了。

1354
00:49:21.720 --> 00:49:22.440
We loved it.
我们很喜欢。

1355
00:49:22.860 --> 00:49:24.900
And everyone, that is the fire.
各位，那才是真正的火。

1356
00:49:25.120 --> 00:49:26.960
I want to leave you with this final moment.
最后我想给你们留下这个瞬间。

1357
00:49:27.300 --> 00:49:34.220
When Rain, as Dwight, sings the song in the conference room, he's holding up the charred cheese pita, whatever.
当雷恩饰演的德怀特在会议室唱歌时，他手里拿着那个烧焦的奶酪皮塔饼之类的东西。

1358
00:49:34.220 --> 00:49:39.840
You can tell when Rain gets through the whole thing, he's so happy.
你能看出来当雷恩唱完那一整段时，他有多开心。

1359
00:49:40.520 --> 00:49:41.540
I want to know.
我想知道。

1360
00:49:41.700 --> 00:49:45.140
I want to text Rain and ask him how many takes did he have to do?
我想给雷恩发短信问问他拍了多少条才过？

1361
00:49:45.420 --> 00:49:49.020
Because when he hits that final, Ryan started the fire.
因为当他唱到最后那句“瑞安点燃了火”时。

1362
00:49:49.320 --> 00:49:54.060
He's like, he's like alive because I think it probably took a few takes to get it.
他看起来，他看起来就像活过来了一样，因为我觉得这可能拍了好几次才成功。

1363
00:49:54.160 --> 00:49:55.320
I bet you're probably right.
我敢说你大概是对的。

1364
00:49:55.760 --> 00:49:56.300
All right.
好的。

1365
00:49:56.460 --> 00:50:00.880
Next week, everybody, we are going to be talking about Halloween.
下周，各位，我们要聊聊《万圣节》那一集。

1366
00:50:01.280 --> 00:50:02.600
Oh, it's special gueSt.
哦，还有特别嘉宾。

1367
00:50:02.920 --> 00:50:04.080
Yes, my neighbor.
没错，我的邻居。

1368
00:50:04.220 --> 00:50:07.420
And the delightful Creed Bratton.
还有可爱的克里德·布拉顿。

1369
00:50:07.640 --> 00:50:10.320
So be sure to join us for that and we'll see you soon.
所以一定要加入我们，我们很快再见。

1370
00:50:10.460 --> 00:50:10.820
Okay, bye.
好的，再见。

1371
